<title>GERMANY: ABN-AMRO says D.Telekom &quot;undervalued&quot;.</title>
<headline>ABN-AMRO says D.Telekom &quot;undervalued&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>ABN-AMRO Hoare Govett analysts have rated shares in German telecommunications group Deutsche Telekom AG as &quot;undervalued&quot;.</p>
<p>Analyst James Ross told Reuters he believed Telekom stock had performed well since its initial public offering in November and that his recommendation put the stock at a &quot;hold/buy&quot;.</p>
<p>He declined to elaborate further.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, 49 228 2609750</p>
</text>
